**Exploring optimization techniques**

I’m considering whether I can use a continuous field gradient in conjunction with a scipy optimizer to assess discrete coordinate derivatives. The field bits are set at 256, and evaluating all flips takes about 28ms. I'm also thinking about using a steepest descent method with a few sweeps, maybe applying basin hopping. It seems that running optimizations with regular random acceptance and parallel chains can get stuck, so I should inspect the best field with matrix and spectral methods to improve my results.
